+## Current activation (momentum transaction-cost sensitivity on the collected universe — R-001, run 45962051330, agent 02)
+
+Ran the decision-relevant cost-robustness qualification of the admitted
+short-horizon momentum candidate (activations 37318950814 / 37361000967): does
+the positive REGIME_STABLE edge survive realistic execution costs, or is it a
+gross-only artifact? Bounded, predeclared cost grid on the SAME signal,
+universe, walk-forward windows, volatility-block regime family, and matched
+coin-flip null as the lookback sweep, so the zero-cost column is directly
+comparable to the admitted evidence. New artifacts:
+`research/checks/momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (check),
+`research/checks/verify_momentum_cost_sensitivity.py` (independent verifier),
+`state/check_artifacts/momentum_cost_sensitivity_results.json` (artifact). No
+framework files were modified; the check reuses `stress_segments` /
+`noise_benchmark` with a cost `BacktestConfig`.
+
+Method: seed 42; dataset yf-ohlcv-universe-2009-to-2026-10-03; lookbacks {3, 5,
+10}; cost levels {zero, realistic, stress2x} where realistic is the repository's
+existing model (commission_per_trade=2.0, commission_per_share=0.003,
+slippage_cents=2.0, slippage_proportional=0.0005) and stress2x doubles every
+component; walk-forward per segment train=252d/test=84d/warmup=60d/overlap=60d;
+4 contiguous volatility blocks; min 400 bars/segment; each (asset, lookback,
+cost) candidate compared vs a coin-flip null run under the SAME cost cfg.
+
+A-priori prediction (declared before the full grid; mechanism-based): the 1-day
+momentum signal has LOW turnover (its sign is persistent over 2009-2026, so the
+constant-dollar rebalancing cost is small relative to the multi-percent per-fold
+edge); prediction COST_ROBUST at realistic costs for the six previously-admitted
+assets, with 2x stress not erasing the edge. Falsification condition: realistic
+costs cutting positive-REGIME_STABLE lookbacks to <2 for a majority of admitted
+assets. A-priori per-asset classification: NO_BASELINE_EDGE if n_edge[zero]==0;
+COST_ROBUST if n_edge[zero]>=2 and n_edge[realistic]>=2; COST_FRAGILE if
+n_edge[realistic]==1; COST_ERASES_EDGE if n_edge[realistic]==0.
+
+Results (seed 42, 10 collected tickers):
+- Classification counts: COST_ROBUST=6 (AAPL, MSFT, GOOGL, AMZN, META, TSLA),
+  NO_BASELINE_EDGE=4 (NVDA, JPM, JNJ, XOM), COST_FRAGILE=0, COST_ERASES_EDGE=0.
+  The COST_ROBUST set is exactly the six assets admitted as lookback-robust in
+  37361000967; the NO_BASELINE_EDGE set is exactly the prior NO_EDGE /
+  regime-dependent assets.
+- Cost drag (mean over segments of zero-cost minus realistic median, lookback 5)
+  is 0.0000 for every asset except NVDA (+0.009, which has no baseline edge);
+  candidate segment medians are essentially IDENTICAL across zero / realistic /
+  stress2x (e.g. META [0.073, 0.067, 0.042] and TSLA [0.132, 0.016, 0.107] at
+  all three levels). Costs are genuinely charged (AAPL realistic commission
+  $18.7k over 4452 rebalancing fills; full-sample total return +553.0% zero ->
+  +551.4% realistic) but are small relative to the edge.
+- Turnover diagnostic: ~1 sign flip per asset over 4465 bars (NVDA 2), i.e. the
+  signal is operationally a persistent LONG for these trending large-caps over
+  the sample; ~3600-4450 constant-dollar rebalancing fills per asset.
+
+Independent verification (three gates, fresh path without `stress_segments`):
+Gate 1 fresh `walk_forward` + `noise_benchmark` recomputation of AMZN/JPM for
+all lookbacks and all cost levels MATCH the artifact (medians, null medians,
+candidate/null dispersion, verdict); Gate 2 the zero-cost column reproduces
+`momentum_lookback_sweep_results.json` on all 10 assets / 3 lookbacks (medians +
+nulls); Gate 3 the per-asset classification and n_edge re-derive from the
+artifact via the documented rule, cost params match, and AMZN lookback-5
+realistic recomputation is identical across reruns. Full regression suite: 168
+tests, all passing.
+
+Verdict: the admitted short-horizon momentum edge is COST_ROBUST — it survives
+the repository's realistic cost model and a 2x conservative stress without
+material degradation of the candidate medians, for exactly the six assets already
+admitted. Decision-relevant qualifications (recorded, not resolved): (1) the
+robustness is a consequence of LOW TURNOVER — the signal is a persistent long
+bias over 2009-2026, so this is NOT a stringent test of a high-turnover timing
+alpha; (2) the regime-verdict machinery is null-dispersion-sensitive (the coin-flip
+null trades far more than the signal and its dispersion changes under costs, so
+n_edge can shift by ±1 without any candidate-median change — e.g. MSFT lookback-5
+zero=REGIME_STABLE vs realistic=REGIME_DEPENDENT on identical medians
+[0.052, 0.072]); the candidate-median invariance, not the n_edge count, is the
+primary evidence; (3) the result remains exploratory research simulation, not a
+traded idea. Frontier update: the cost-robustness qualification of the momentum
+candidate is now closed (COST_ROBUST); the momentum cell remains admitted as
+candidate positive evidence, now cost-classified. The next decision-relevant
+frontier cells are the predeclared holding-period (R-002) and volatility-gate
+(R-003) qualifications, then a genuinely new signal class.
+
+---
+
